# pipe_prose

## `parseExpr`

```
parseExpr : String -> Int
```

Parse an expression.

  The marker above sits on the SECOND line of this doc block: the
  decorative separator on the line before it is a separate comment that
  `findDocForLine`'s proximity rule merged in.  It is still stripped.

  The rows below are USER CONTENT and must survive verbatim:

  ```
  expr ::= term
  ```

| expr | term |
|------|------|
| a    | b    |

## `otherEntry`

```
otherEntry : Int -> Int
```

A second marked block, to show the marker is consumed once per BLOCK and
  not once per file.

| still | a | table |

